Description: Small tools for working with coding agents
 agent-install prints the command that installs Claude Code, Codex or
 Antigravity CLI from its vendor's native installer, set up so the
 installer leaves shell startup files alone.
 .
 agent-ps lists running Claude Code and Codex processes with their
 working directory, age, tty and tmux pane. Detection is process-based
 (ps and /proc), and Claude rows are enriched from the per-session
 metadata Claude Code writes under ~/.claude/sessions.
 .
 claude-sync syncs Claude Code sessions between two machines over ssh
 and rsync, so a session can be resumed on either one.
 .
 claude-user runs Claude Code as the account (work, personal, ...) that
 the current directory belongs to, each with its own config dir.

